  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sq_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Step Sequencer\n\nA tone matrix: 16 steps × 8 notes of a scale. Click a cell to switch it on or off, drag to paint a run of them; the playhead sweeps left to right and every lit cell in its column plays (up to four at once). R scatters a random tune, C (or the Clear bang) empties the grid. Tempo, Tone (the filter) and the Scale are on the canvas.\n\nHow it works: the grid is a State* of 128 on/off values, rewritten by one Expression each frame (the cell under a press takes the paint value). A phase accumulator counts sixteenth notes; on each new step the lit rows of the column become notes (Scale), shared out to four MonoSynth voices, which Mix into one filter, delay and reverb.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sq_mouse",
      "defType": "input/mouse",
      "position": {
        "x": 37,
        "y": 382
      },
      "params": {}
    },
